Author: Danny Milosavljevic <dannym@friendly-machines.com>
Date: 2026-04-20
Subject: Fix wrong record-type casts and PPU-loader type confusion
License: expat

The FPC 1.0.6 compiler has wrong casts that native FPC tolerated
by coincidence and the tp2cc-translated bootstrap exposes:

 * Source-level casts that lie about the record type at the cast
   site -- e.g. casting a tprocsym pointer as pvarsym, casting an
   ait_symbol_end record as pai_symbol, casting the Val call node's
   resulttype as pfloatdef.  The cast names a record type that has
   nothing to do with the actual record at the address.  Native FPC
   only got away with these because the surrounding code happened
   to read a field at an offset that the wrong record also has, or
   because the variant-part bytes happened to land on a tolerated
   value.  Under tp2cc the translated emitter renders a narrowing cast
   between unrelated record types as a checked downcast, and the
   sized allocation no longer accommodates the over-read.

 * PPU-loader placeholders.  The loader stored a `tderef' helper
   chain (the unresolved cross-reference cookie) directly in fields
   declared as the resolved subtype -- ptypesym, pprocdef,
   pobjectdef, penumdef, ppropertysym -- treating the field as
   temporary cookie storage until `deref' replaced the cookie with
   a real pointer.  That in-place reuse claimed the field already
   held the resolved type when in fact it held a tderef of an
   entirely different record type (no shared hierarchy with the
   declared type).  The translated bootstrap then issued a
   class-hierarchy downcast on a foreign object.  Restructured to park the chain
   in a shadow `pderef' field instead, leaving the typed field nil
   until `deref' runs.  PPU on-disk format is unchanged --
   `writederef' synthesises the bytes from the live object after
   `deref', never from the chain.

Site-by-site summary:

 * i386/aggas.pas, ait_symbol_end branch: cast was
   pai_symbol(hp) where hp^.typ=ait_symbol_end.  Both records
   happen to expose a `sym' field at the same offset so the
   wrong cast read the right bytes; the correct cast is
   pai_symbol_end.

 * i386/aggas.pas, ait_align branch: on i386 the align records are
   split into a shared tai_align_abstract base in aasm.pas and a
   cpu-specific tai_align child in cpuasm.pas.  This branch only
   reads the shared base fields (aligntype/use_op/fillop), so the
   historic pai_align(hp) narrowing is both unnecessary and wrong
   when the list node is only a tai_align_abstract.  Read it through
   pai_align_abstract instead.

 * i386/cginl.pas, Handle_Val, floatdef branch: cast was
   pfloatdef(p^.resulttype) but p is the whole Val call node --
   its resulttype is the procedure return type, not the
   destination variable's type.  Use dest_para^.resulttype
   instead, matching the outer case.

 * i386/cginl.pas, inc/dec pointerdef branch: the old
   `porddef(ppointerdef(... )^.pointertype.def)=voiddef` cast narrows the
   pointee type to torddef just to compare it with the builtin `voiddef`.
   That is wrong for pointers-to-pointers and other non-orddef pointees.
   Compare the `pdef` directly to `pdef(voiddef)` instead.

 * i386/cgflw.pas, `secondfor': `is_signed' already accepts a `pdef` and
   handles both orddefs and enumdefs.  The old `porddef(p^.t2^.resulttype)`
   wrapper wrongly narrows enum loop variables to torddef first.

 * pexpr.pas (2 sites inside typesym member-read handling):
   `sym' is already declared `psym' in the enclosing function;
   the historic `pvarsym(..)' wrap around `srsymtable^.search(..)'
   and `search_class_member(..)' was a narrowing to a sibling
   record (not a hierarchy descent) and did nothing useful since
   the call sites only read psym-level fields afterwards.
   Dropped.

 * pexpr.pas, `is_func_ret' branch: the historic identity tests
   `pfuncretsym(sym)=...` and `pvarsym(sym)=opsym` narrow a generic
   `psym` to unrelated sibling record types just to compare pointer
   identity. Under tp2cc those become checked downcasts on objects
   of the wrong dynamic type, e.g. a `tfuncretsym' masquerading as
   `tvarsym'. Compare at the common `psym' level instead.

 * tcadd.pas, set-operation handling: when a type-mismatch
   between `rd' and a setdef `ld' was reported via CGMessage the
   code fell through without halting, then later did
   `psetdef(rd)^.settype' on a non-setdef `rd'.  Guard the
   psetdef(rd) cast with `(rd^.deftype=setdef)'.

 * tree.pas, genloadnode: the parameter is typed pvarsym but some
   callers (e.g. the `constresourcestring' branch in pexpr) pass
   a tconstsym expecting the caller to set p^.resulttype
   themselves.  Guard the `v^.vartype.def' read to the subtypes
   that actually have a `vartype' field (tvarsym and its child
   tabsolutesym).

 * tree.pas, genprocinlinenode: `calln.symtableprocentry` was widened to
   `psym`, but this site only accepts procedure symbols. Cast it back to
   `pprocsym` here instead of narrowing the whole call-node field again.

 * tccnv.pas / tcmem.pas, proc-to-procvar conversion: these helper calls
   also expect a `pprocsym`.  Keep `calln.symtableprocentry` widened to
   `psym`, but cast it back at the proc-only `get_proc_2_procvar_def`
   call sites.

 * tree.pas, `disposetree' `dt_with' branch: like `tcmem.firstwith',
   the old loop advanced once past the last real `withsymtable`
   entry via `pwithsymtable(symt^.next)` even though that value was
   never consumed afterwards.  On the final iteration `next` is the
   ordinary `symtablestack` tail, not another `withsymtable`, so the
   translated downcast lands on the wrong dynamic type. Stop
   advancing after the last real `withsymtable`.

 * tcmem.pas, `firstwith': the loop walks exactly `tablecount`
   `withsymtable` entries, but the old code still advanced once
   past the last one via `pwithsymtable(symtable^.next)` even
   though the value was never used afterwards. For a single-entry
   `with`, that `next` pointer is already the ordinary
   `symtablestack` tail, not another `withsymtable`, so the
   translated checked downcast lands on the wrong dynamic type. Only advance
   when another `withsymtable` iteration remains.

 * symdefh.inc / symsymh.inc: add shadow `pderef' fields
   alongside every PPU-reference field that held a pderef
   placeholder: tdef.typesym_deref, tenumdef.basedef_deref,
   tprocdef.nextoverloaded_deref, tprocdef._class_deref,
   tobjectdef.childof_deref, tprocsym.definition_deref,
   tpropertysym.propoverriden_deref, tenumsym.definition_deref.

 * symdef.inc / symsym.inc: each affected `load' now parks the
   readderef chain in the shadow and leaves the typed field nil;
   each affected `deref' moves the chain back into the typed
   field (a cast between unrelated record types, which the
   translated emitter renders as a reinterpret) and runs the upstream
   in-place resolve unchanged.

